abstract: >
  BrainDrop is a free, open-source AI-powered study companion for Indian
  school students preparing for CBSE board examinations. It integrates four
  large language models (NVIDIA Llama 3.3 70B, Groq Llama 3.3, Google
  Gemini 2.5 Flash, Anthropic Claude Haiku 4.5) with a client-side TF-IDF
  RAG pipeline over NCERT textbook content. Distinctive features include a
  multi-agent classroom mode (grade-specific Teacher plus Classmates with
  separate personalities), AI-generated interactive HTML simulations called
  MagicBlocks, and the "Quiet Competence" design system that deliberately
  rejects the gamified-celebration aesthetic typical of category-leading
  EdTech apps. The project ships with no API keys in the browser; all model
  calls route through a Cloudflare Worker proxy.
